    "result": "Static IDA review confirms the same 12-byte DFSE2 key domain, seven clean verdict bytes, zero separators, big-endian length framing, SHA-256 and xorshift stream as the reviewed Windows implementations. The 91-byte SPKI reconstructed from native constants matches the existing ECDSA-P256 verifier key. Environment framing, signed length 18432, P1363 r/s fields and signed seed binding at 0x4000 match the managed validator.",
